  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires all thermal incidents reported within 24 hours and customer notice within 48 hours. S2 weakens the 5% test limit into an action threshold with no automatic sales ban, while providing per-model results to customers and regulators but not the general public. S3 sets a 6-year retrofit deadline with a feasibility escape; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notice but no transition period."
